# interplay_limits_child_wait_alias_dies: Two waiters whose ids differ by 32 kill the host: child 1 waits on the root's next stamp (bit 1), then child 33 waits on it too, marks bit 1 again, and DeviceCore::add_wait's check that the waiter's bit is clear in the waiting word dies, in every setup (the device is the host's). The root and child 32 alias the same way (interplay_limits_root_wait_alias_dies). Child 33 reaches its wait only after an 8 MiB NOP, so the death lands in the wait after its doorbell.
